# Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-GPTQ-Int4  —  DP2 x TP4  (THE aggregate-throughput lever)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two independent TP=4 replicas across all 8 Gaudi cards (cards 0-3 = r0, 4-7 = r1),
# fronted by dp_serve.sh's nginx least_conn balancer. Each replica is a FULL model
# copy on 4 cards serving whole requests by itself. Measured: TP=4 gets ~2x the
# per-request throughput of TP=8 (less collective tax, fatter per-card compute) but
# uses only 4 cards; running TWO replicas reclaims the other 4 cards -> ~2x aggregate
# throughput vs a single TP=4, and beats the TP=8 single instance (which tops ~206
# tok/s @C250 and is collective-bound) at high concurrency.
#
# LAUNCH (manual DP via dp_serve.sh — the proven path; in-engine --data-parallel-size
# is non-functional on this build):
#     ./dp_serve.sh qwen35-397b-dp2tp4 dp2_tp4
# dp_serve.sh strips --tensor-parallel-size from VLLM_ARGS and sets TP=4 per replica;
# it KEEPS --enable-expert-parallel for TP>1 (each replica does EP across its own 4
# cards: ep_size=4, local_num_experts=128/4=32). The warm-first flow compiles r0,
# then fans out r1 sharing r0's recipe cache read-only.
#
# REQUIRES the DP+EP expert-id fix (patches/dp_ep_dispatch_fix.patch) applied to the
# mounted hpu-moe-ext: without it, EP under the DP flatten maps a GLOBAL expert id
# onto a LOCAL 32-element param -> IndexError at load. (With manual DP each replica is
# contiguous EP-at-TP4 and the patch's authoritative-expert_map remap is exact.)
#
# 220GB int4 weights / 4 cards = 55GB/card; bf16/torch.compile (PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0,
# required on this upstream-PyTorch base image). HIGH-CONCURRENCY profile: prefix
# caching OFF (dodges the Qwen3.5 GDN/mamba chunk-align crash @C>=100), max-num-seqs
# 256, 8K ctx, async scheduling. NOTE: this is multimodal (Qwen3.5-VL) — TP=4 also
# keeps the vision merger linear input (4608) group_size(128)-aligned (4608/4=1152).
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:1.24
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-GPTQ-Int4
SERVED_NAME=qwen35-397b
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=900 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000"
# --tensor-parallel-size is STRIPPED by dp_serve.sh (it sets TP=4 per replica). Keep
# --enable-expert-parallel (dp_serve preserves it for TP>1). No repack cache here: do
# NOT set HPU_MOE_REPACK_LOAD to a cache minted under a different EP layout (e.g. TP=8,
# 16/rank) — mint a fresh DP2xTP4 cache or run uncached (eager repacks live at load).
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization gptq_hpu --tensor-parallel-size 4 --enable-expert-parallel --max-model-len 8192 --max-num-seqs 256 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
